   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">Dear all,</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br>I wanted to ask a question regarding confirmatory factor analysis step in genomicSEM: </div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\">On genomicSEM github</span><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"> </span><a title=\"https://github.com/GenomicSEM/GenomicSEM/wiki/3.-Genome%E2%80%90wide-Models\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/GenomicSEM/GenomicSEM/wiki/3.-Genome%E2%80%90wide-Models\" style=\"font:inherit;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/GenomicSEM/GenomicSEM/wiki/3.-Genome%25E2%2580%2590wide-Models&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237033149000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NBrbCuGwKOnC1nNv_g7Fg\">wik</a><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\">i I found mentioning concerning running EFA step: &quot;</span><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"><i>Below we provide an example of a workflow in which we do not have an a priori model, and therefore first conduct an exploratory factor analysis before specifying and fitting a usermodel.</i></span><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"> &quot; I understood that running EFA is then only recommended if the researcher is not able to determine a factor model based on theory or previous work, did I understood this correctly? As I am working with internalizing and externalizing behaviour, we can have a priori two factor model with externalizing factor and internalizing factor.</span></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">When I run CFA on this two factor model and look at output of CFA I observe the following model fit:</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i>Externalizing_factor=~ NA *trait1 + trait2 +trait3 + trait4  + trait5 + trait6 + trait7 + trait8</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i>Internalizing_factor=~ NA * trait8 +  trait9 + trait10 +trait11 + trait12<br>F1~~F2<br>F1~~1*F1<br>F2~~1*F2&quot;</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i><br></i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i>$modelfit</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.66666;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black;direction:ltr\"><i> chisq df p_chisq       AIC            CFI             SRMR</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.66666;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black;direction:ltr\"><i>df 2967.64 52       0 3019.64 0.7839851 0.1661678</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.66666;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black;direction:ltr\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">Based on previous work and posts in GenomicSEM users group, I understood that this is a poor model fit and therefore should not continue with this model (as CFI is below 0.9 and SRMR above 0.1). However, the residual covariance matrix shows good fit as the highest value I observe is  1.578590e-02 (based on $resid_cov$`Residual Covariance Matrix: Calculated as Observed Cov - Model Implied Cov`output)</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">In the following<a title=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2435310/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2435310/\" style=\"border:0px;font:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2435310/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237033149000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2xRGATaKzuyrfEqYs9vGLi\"> paper</a> I read that there could be cases where residuals and model fit are not compatible.  However, I am not certain that a model with not good/acceptable fit indices in genomicSEM is reliable and good model to run multivariate GWAS, even when the residuals are minimal.</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">If the model fit is not optimal but residuals do show good fit, should the choice of model for multivariate GWAS be based on the residual covariance matrix, on biological interest/research question in including certain traits in the model (despite having poor model fit) or only on the model fit?</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">Thank you very much in advance for your time and advice!</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "RZ3T60LyAwAJ",
   "from": "Elliot Tucker-Drob",
   "author": "ac421cf36d1a4c37",
   "date": "2025-06-30T14:33:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: GenomicSEM: model fit and Residual Covariance Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The unstandardized residual matrix can be misleading with respect to model fit for phenotypes with low h2. You can compute the model residuals for the standardized S matrix to put the residuals on a more interpretable scale that is more comparable to the scale of SRMR.</div><div>Your model has a lot of traits and imposes simple structure; I suspect that cross-loadings may be useful to improve fit.</div><div>You can see how we did something similar (start with a theory-derived model imposing simple structure, then using model esiduals to identify cross-loadings to free) in the ReGPC supplement (see &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">Genomic SEM Analyses Stratified by Measurement Instrument&quot;)</span>: <a href=\"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.05.16.648988v1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.05.16.648988v1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237033153000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ypZydw8Ym-im88CAeqG2M\">https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.05.16.648988v1</a></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nYavor Dragostinov conducted those analyses, so after reading through that section, you might reach out to him if you have questions.<div><br><div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Jun 30, 2025 at 4:25 AM B &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">barbar...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">Dear all,</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br>I wanted to ask a question regarding confirmatory factor analysis step in genomicSEM: </div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\">On genomicSEM github</span><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"> </span><a title=\"https://github.com/GenomicSEM/GenomicSEM/wiki/3.-Genome%E2%80%90wide-Models\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://github.com/GenomicSEM/GenomicSEM/wiki/3.-Genome%E2%80%90wide-Models\" style=\"font:inherit;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/GenomicSEM/GenomicSEM/wiki/3.-Genome%25E2%2580%2590wide-Models&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237033153000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1d2fdtP686NpDqDyXYWE2D\">wik</a><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\">i I found mentioning concerning running EFA step: &quot;</span><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"><i>Below we provide an example of a workflow in which we do not have an a priori model, and therefore first conduct an exploratory factor analysis before specifying and fitting a usermodel.</i></span><span style=\"color:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-size:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-variant-ligatures:inherit;font-variant-caps:inherit;font-weight:inherit\"> &quot; I understood that running EFA is then only recommended if the researcher is not able to determine a factor model based on theory or previous work, did I understood this correctly? As I am working with internalizing and externalizing behaviour, we can have a priori two factor model with externalizing factor and internalizing factor.</span></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">When I run CFA on this two factor model and look at output of CFA I observe the following model fit:</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i>Externalizing_factor=~ NA *trait1 + trait2 +trait3 + trait4  + trait5 + trait6 + trait7 + trait8</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i>Internalizing_factor=~ NA * trait8 +  trait9 + trait10 +trait11 + trait12<br>F1~~F2<br>F1~~1*F1<br>F2~~1*F2&quot;</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i><br></i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><i>$modelfit</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.66666;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black;direction:ltr\"><i> chisq df p_chisq       AIC            CFI             SRMR</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.66666;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black;direction:ltr\"><i>df 2967.64 52       0 3019.64 0.7839851 0.1661678</i></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.66666;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black;direction:ltr\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">Based on previous work and posts in GenomicSEM users group, I understood that this is a poor model fit and therefore should not continue with this model (as CFI is below 0.9 and SRMR above 0.1). However, the residual covariance matrix shows good fit as the highest value I observe is  1.578590e-02 (based on $resid_cov$`Residual Covariance Matrix: Calculated as Observed Cov - Model Implied Cov`output)</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">In the following<a title=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2435310/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2435310/\" style=\"border:0px;font:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2435310/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237033153000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kn7v8xdVEfr8vEj22UsMh\"> paper</a> I read that there could be cases where residuals and model fit are not compatible.  However, I am not certain that a model with not good/acceptable fit indices in genomicSEM is reliable and good model to run multivariate GWAS, even when the residuals are minimal.</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">If the model fit is not optimal but residuals do show good fit, should the choice of model for multivariate GWAS be based on the residual covariance matrix, on biological interest/research question in including certain traits in the model (despite having poor model fit) or only on the model fit?</div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\"><br></div><div style=\"border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;font-size:12pt;line-height:inherit;font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size-adjust:inherit;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:black\">Thank you very much in advance for your time and advice!</div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Genomic SEM Users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">genomic-sem-us...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/genomic-sem-users/56989cb0-e980-4e23-abb4-d11fef89fa7fn%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/genomic-sem-users/56989cb0-e980-4e23-abb4-d11fef89fa7fn%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237033153000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZAUtzJGhwJ1HluIIik29w\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/genomic-sem-users/56989cb0-e980-4e23-abb4-d11fef89fa7fn%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div>\r\n"
